.el .ds Aq '
.TH mdmc-reconcile 1  "reconcile " 
.SH NAME
mdmc\-reconcile \- Sync draft status with the maildirs (forward\-only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmdmc reconcile\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sync draft status with the maildirs (forward\-only)
.PP
Marks a draft `pending` when its message\-id is in the account\*(Aqs drafts maildir, and `sent` when it is in the sent maildir. Never downgrades: `pending` is not regressed to `draft`, and `sent` is terminal. A message found in both drafts and sent is marked `sent` with a warning about the stale drafts copy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config.toml (default ~/.config/mdmc/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
